{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CAREGIVER): We were ages getting in. The traffic on the N7 was desperate, bumper to bumper from the Red Cow.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ah I know, I was late myself. Was it the rain?",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Rain, and then the sun came out, typical. The grandson had hurling in the park after, they were beaten by two points, and he's only eight.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Two points, sure that's close enough. Right, sorry, this yoke is frozen. What has you in?",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Stomach pain.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Stomach pain. Where, sorry, say that again.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Here.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Right side, up under the ribs. It comes on after a fatty meal and it lasts for hours.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): Fatty meals. Err. How long does the pain stay?",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (PATIENT): Hours.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (CAREGIVER): A few hours, then it settles. It's been about three months.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sorry, three months did you say? The screen jumped.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Three months, yes.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Umm. Was there vomiting?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): Once.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Only the once. She had the rashers and eggs and she vomited after.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever with these spells?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any yellow colour in the eyes or the skin?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Loose stools?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): What about passing water, any bother?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Grand. Of. Medicines, what are you taking?",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (CAREGIVER): She's on Mizartan for the blood pressure, 40 milligrams in the morning.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mizartan, sorry, what dose, say it again.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Forty milligrams, every morning. She has the high blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): And an antacid, is it?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): Gaviscon.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (CAREGIVER): A spoon of Gaviscon after a fatty meal. It takes the edge off a small bit. And Omprazole, 20 milligrams every morning for the stomach.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): Omprazole twenty, every morning. Right. Any allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (CAREGIVER): None that I know of.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): Your mother, the gallbladder, was that mentioned at the desk or am I mixing people up?",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Her mother had the gallbladder taken out, years ago.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. And the tablets in the bag on the chair, are those hers?",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Ah no, the Metformine is her husband's, for his sugar. And the biotin is my sister's, for the hair. Neither of them is hers.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (DOCTOR): Grand so, not yours. Do you smoke?",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll have a feel of the tummy if that's alright. Sorry, one second, the cursor's gone again.",
  "[SEG0043] person_2 (DOCTOR): Abdomen is soft. Tender under the right ribs. No guarding.",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (PATIENT): Sore.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. I think this is probably biliary colic, gallstones, though we'll see what the tests say before anyone calls it certain.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll book blood tests, a full blood count and liver tests, and an ultrasound of the gallbladder.",
  "[SEG0047] person_2 (DOCTOR): Lay off the fry-ups till we know. Come back in two weeks for the results. If the pain turns savage or you go yellow, go to A&E, don't wait.",
  "[SEG0048] person_1 (CAREGIVER): Grand, we'll do that. The bus home should be quieter now the match is over.",
  "[SEG0049] person_3 (PATIENT): Grand.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right so. Mind yourselves on the way out.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (CAREGIVER): We will. Thanks."
 ],
